  "findings": [
    "Existing comment/history/mention/list grants remain canonical. New14 rules/claims/per-user preferences/reference-only notice metadata join I01 and the shared AppJobs/legacy push outbox; no duplicate scheduler/provider gateway.",
    "Current Task edits synchronously cancel/re-anchor pending reminders; injected observer/native faults roll back Task/claim/notice mutations. Assignment/reassignment notifications also join the Task command and stable identity.",
    "A real restore test with deliberately different snapshot/restore clocks initially replayed a delayed digest. Shared synchronous minimum-version domain restore policies now consume pending notice references inside replacement COMMIT, preserving inbox history and fencing old epoch jobs. A failing policy rolls back replacement; this is not a timestamp-only guess.",
    "Two review findings have three actual RED assertions: UTC spelling created distinct reminder identities/SDK acknowledgement mismatch, and256-character preserved Task IDs exceeded the shared job-key limit. Canonical millisecond UTC and bounded hashed continuation keys fix the causes; no assertion/timeout/retry relaxation.",
    "One subsequent fixture claim-count failure was an earlier test’s synthetic restore marker surviving a clock reset. Each owned notification fixture now resets that marker; all assertions remain unchanged.",
    "Quiet hours and daily digest use explicit named-zone real instants, including overnight/half-hour/DST gap/fold cases. External push is retryable/outcome-unknown per shared ownership; only inbox identity is deduped, never an exactly-once provider receipt promise.",
    "Current recipient/source access is rechecked before dispatch and again before external push. Deleted recipients are suppressed without blocking live recipients. A digest stays visible only while at least one current source is readable.",
    "Task reminder/own Settings packets retain original revisions/body/key through lost acknowledgements and navigation. Unsent own settings also survive unrelated Task SSE; Task visibility loss/logout fence late continuations. No browser offline writes or real provider/test push."
  ],
